    {
      "post_id": "552842642216988672",
      "text": "Oh, and the cover of today's edition of Charlie Hebdo mocked Michel Houellebecq for writing an Islamophobic novel... http://t.co/moLfdEMlpM",
      "timestamp": "Wed Jan 07 15:02:11 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": null,
      "post_type": "source"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553273933269463041",
      "text": "@DougSaunders this is a matter of opinion and general take on things too @its_georgie101 @left_liberal",
      "timestamp": "Thu Jan 08 19:35:59 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.5327208207181824e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553277880453836800",
      "text": "@its_georgie101 @left_liberal @facepalmidiots No, they want to see a gesture of solidarity with people who were killed for their work.",
      "timestamp": "Thu Jan 08 19:51:40 +0000 2015",
      "parent_id": 5.532777019228938e+17,
      "post_type": "reaction"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "553276034268012544",
      "text": "@facepalmidiots @its_georgie101 @left_liberal I don't think it's illegitimate to find their work racially offensive,even if it's complicated",
